      "conditions": ["Material facts, dependencies or governing assumptions change."],
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 856,
          "quote": "Excluding a check requires supported dependency coverage and a reason the change\ncannot invalidate the reused claim. An absent edge proves no non-influence.\nUnknown impact widens assessment or leaves the dependent assurance unresolved.\nNew obligations and uncovered cases create assessment work even when no existing\ncheck covers them; mandatory gates remain applicable. Selection itself produces\nno execution evidence. The representation need not be an exhaustive graph or a\nseparate ledger.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/codex/5592168e26759f37e730aed12c030a6061709ec4/source/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#STDO%20Foundations%2FConstruction%20assurance%2FChange%20impact%20and%20evidence%20retention",
          "start_line": 850
        }
      ],
      "key": "impact_selection_obligations",
      "statement": "The candidate selection is S_Delta = { t : D*(t) intersects I(Delta) }. Requirements-to-test links alone cannot establish complete impact. Exclusion requires supported dependency coverage and a reason the change cannot invalidate reuse; missing edges prove no non-influence. Unknown impact widens assessment or leaves assurance unresolved. New obligations and uncovered cases require work even without existing checks; mandatory gates remain applicable. Selection produces no execution evidence. Selection considers impact analysis, acquisition, execution and assessment costs together, distinguishes estimates from measurements, and remains constrained by required assurance, risk policy and gates; cheap selection cannot leave required obligations uncovered. Broad/uncertain impact, a changed selection model, release rules or missed dependencies can justify wider testing. Full suites can still have gaps; no universal cadence or gate exemption follows. Failures enter diagnosis and authorized response; evidence acquisition may precede justified repair.",
      "uncertainty": ""
    },
    {
      "applies_to_keys": ["change_impact_retention"],
      "conditions": ["Evidence is reused for a new subject and basis."],
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 878,
          "quote": "A relaxed requirement can change what remains owed; it neither makes\nthe former failure a success nor erases it. The changed subject is assessed\nagainst its current obligations with the applicable evidence.",
