          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/codex/5592168e26759f37e730aed12c030a6061709ec4/source/standards/ODD_METHOD.md#ODD%20Method%2F10.%20What%20An%20ODD%20Product%20Is",
          "start_line": 542
        }
      ],
      "key": "odd_topology_frame_separation",
      "statement": "Actual locations bind through stdo_<label>.json. Universal ODD commits to one WHAT surface, one HOW relation, ABG-owned runtime and Product-owned domain meaning, not fixed directories; software-development topology is default only. reference_frame_bases denotes evaluation frames under REFERENCE_FRAME_METHOD. Same-spelled ABG runtime/attention/zoom/overlay frames remain runtime contracts in WHAT/HOW, do not automatically join the collective evaluation set, and may be exact subjects/coordinates of declared evaluation frames without identity collapse.",
      "uncertainty": ""
