      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 624,
          "quote": "An ODD product is built correctly only when all of the following are true.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/codex/5592168e26759f37e730aed12c030a6061709ec4/source/standards/ODD_METHOD.md#ODD%20Method%2F11.%20Core%20Law",
          "start_line": 624
        }
      ],
      "key": "odd_core_conjunctive_requirement",
      "statement": "All following core-law conditions are necessary for ODD correctness. The supplied excerpt includes only part of that following body, so satisfying its local subset cannot establish full correctness.",
      "uncertainty": "Later core-law clauses after 11.5C are absent."
    },
    {
      "applies_to_keys": ["odd_product", "odd_node"],
      "conditions": [],
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 638,
          "quote": "Concrete assets must bind explicitly into typed domain boundaries.\n\nWhere an asset is a real produced or consumed boundary, declare its `asset_surface`.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/codex/5592168e26759f37e730aed12c030a6061709ec4/source/standards/ODD_METHOD.md#ODD%20Method%2F11.%20Core%20Law%2F11.1%20Typed%20Assets%20And%20Nodes%20Are%20Explicit",
          "start_line": 636
        }
      ],
      "key": "explicit_typed_asset_boundaries",
      "statement": "Work must use explicit typed assets/nodes and concrete typed domain bindings, not a hidden project blob, giant mutable workspace object or undocumented service payload. Every real produced/consumed asset boundary declares its asset_surface.",
      "uncertainty": ""
    },
    {
      "applies_to_keys": ["odd_graph_function", "odd_product"],
      "conditions": [],
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 645,
          "quote": "Every operative constructive step is carried by:\n\n- one named `GraphFunction`, or\n- one lawful graph-function composition",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/codex/5592168e26759f37e730aed12c030a6061709ec4/source/standards/ODD_METHOD.md#ODD%20Method%2F11.%20Core%20Law%2F11.2%20Graph%20Functions%20Are%20The%20Primary%20Constructive%20Carrier",
          "start_line": 642
        }
      ],
      "key": "graph_function_carrier_requirement",
      "statement": "Every operative constructive step uses one named GraphFunction or lawful graph-function composition. The real carrier must not remain in orchestration loops, bespoke Python pipeline runners, controller scripts or service methods merely calling GTL-adjacent helpers.",
      "uncertainty": ""
    },
    {
      "applies_to_keys": ["odd_product", "odd_traversal", "odd_graph_function"],
      "conditions": ["ODD uses edge traversal as its compute unit."],
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 663,
          "quote": "The required realization order is:\n\n1. declare the outcome traversal over typed assets\n2. publish the declarative GTL/ABG carrier structure\n3. implement only the minimal imperative adapter code that remains necessary",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/codex/5592168e26759f37e730aed12c030a6061709ec4/source/standards/ODD_METHOD.md#ODD%20Method%2F11.%20Core%20Law%2F11.2A%20Outcome-First%20Realization%20Order",
          "start_line": 659
        }
      ],
      "key": "outcome_first_realization",
      "statement": "The Product must use traversal units to build its operative framework behavior: first declare outcome traversal over typed assets, next publish declarative GTL/ABG structure, then implement only necessary minimal imperative adapters. Before implementation declare source/target types, traversal/function name, closure/evaluation, lineage, ambiguity/gap obligations and allowed F_D/F_P/F_H bindings. Declarative structure includes functions, typed nodes, vectors, operator/evaluator bindings, schemas, policy/projection and lineage-ledger declarations. Imperative-first behavior later decorated with GTL vocabulary is ODD-shaped, not yet ODD-built.",
      "uncertainty": ""
    },
    {
      "applies_to_keys": ["odd_graph_function", "odd_product"],
      "conditions": ["Publishing the live function line."],
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 715,
          "quote": "The live line must publish a machine-readable function catalog.\n\nAt minimum, each retained function should expose:\n\n- name\n- inputs\n- outputs\n- intent\n- public or helper role\n\nIf the callable surface exists only in prose or prompt memory, the product is under-built.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/codex/5592168e26759f37e730aed12c030a6061709ec4/source/standards/ODD_METHOD.md#ODD%20Method%2F11.%20Core%20Law%2F11.3%20The%20Function%20Catalog%20Is%20Published",
          "start_line": 705
        }
      ],
      "key": "function_catalog_publication",
      "statement": "A machine-readable live function catalog must be published. Each retained function should expose at least name, inputs, outputs, intent and public/helper role. Callable surfaces existing only in prose or prompt memory leave the Product under-built.",
      "uncertainty": ""
    },
    {
      "applies_to_keys": ["odd_product", "odd_graph_function", "odd_vector"],
      "conditions": [],
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 730,
          "quote": "Do not bind callers directly to hidden inner vectors.\n\nWhere a public carrier refines into inner executable structure, publish the live traversal boundaries explicitly through lawful GTL boundary surfaces such as `RefinementBoundary` or `CandidateFamily`.\n\nThe outer public carrier remains the callable contract.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/codex/5592168e26759f37e730aed12c030a6061709ec4/source/standards/ODD_METHOD.md#ODD%20Method%2F11.%20Core%20Law%2F11.4%20The%20GTL%20Module%20Is%20The%20Operative%20Publication%20Surface",
          "start_line": 726
        }
      ],
      "key": "gtl_operative_publication",
      "statement": "Publish public graph-function carriers, graphs traversed, typed node/vector surfaces and semantic jobs or equivalent outer callable contracts bound to public carriers. Callers must not bind directly to hidden inner vectors. Refined public carriers require explicit live traversal boundaries through lawful GTL surfaces such as RefinementBoundary or CandidateFamily, while retaining the outer public carrier as callable contract.",
      "uncertainty": "Concrete lawful GTL boundary schemas are not supplied."
    },
    {
      "applies_to_keys": ["odd_product", "abg_runtime_role"],
      "conditions": ["An ODD application operates over GTL/ABG."],
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 786,
          "quote": "If an application attempts to replace ABG continuation with tenant-local\ncontrol flow, it is no longer behaving as an ODD application over GTL/ABG. It\nhas drifted into a different architecture that only happens to publish some\nODD-shaped artifacts.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/codex/5592168e26759f37e730aed12c030a6061709ec4/source/standards/ODD_METHOD.md#ODD%20Method%2F11.%20Core%20Law%2F11.5A%20ABG%20Owns%20Continuation%20And%20Re-Entry",
          "start_line": 783
        }
      ],
      "key": "abg_continuation_exclusivity",
      "statement": "The application is a cooperative subsystem. ABG owns continuation authority, publish-boundary re-entry, graph-call lifecycle and step selection. The Product must not own hidden continuation loops, retain multi-step controller memory across publish boundaries, infer later steps locally instead of ABG re-entry, treat public next and explicit graph-function continuation as rival authorities, or replace ABG with local orchestration. Such replacement is a different architecture, even if it emits ODD-shaped artifacts.",
      "uncertainty": ""
    },
    {
      "applies_to_keys": ["odd_product", "abg_runtime_role"],
      "conditions": ["An ODD Product changes runtime, start/iterate, worker transport, actor invocation, process supervision, plugin dispatch, event projection, closure, assurance, retry or continuation semantics."],
      "exceptions": ["A different realization is lawful only in an explicitly ratified, non-overlapping runtime scope."],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 800,
          "quote": "The audit must prove that there is exactly one execution authority for the\naffected traversal. For a consumer using the GTL and ABG roles, that authority\nis the one consumer-bound realization of the ABG role. This remains true when\nthe realization under change itself implements that role. A different\nrealization is lawful only under an explicitly ratified, non-overlapping\nruntime scope.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/codex/5592168e26759f37e730aed12c030a6061709ec4/source/standards/ODD_METHOD.md#ODD%20Method%2F11.%20Core%20Law%2F11.5B%20Execution%20Authority%20Audit",
          "start_line": 795
        }
      ],
      "key": "execution_authority_audit",
      "statement": "Before activation and closure, audit exactly one authority for every affected traversal: the consumer-bound ABG realization, even when that realization itself is being changed. Inventory at least: traversal/vector advance (Product declares graphs/assets/policy; no local next-step runner); actor invocation/supervision (Product provides bindings/prompts/payload/evidence adapters; no spawn/spawnSync/exec/timeout/kill/stdout/stderr supervision outside ABG actor seam); retry/correction/continuation/re-entry (bounded outputs and return control; no retry loops/controller memory/hidden next); runtime event emission/append/replay/projection (map evidence to admitted payloads; no direct append, side ledgers or reconstruction bypass); closure/assurance (ABG with domain policy/gain; Product supplies interpretation/evaluators/gaps/weights, not self-report/postflight closure). Consequential entity-transformation admission specializes STDO-UP-016, without reclassifying ABG's broader execution/supervision/retry/projection authority as admission. F_P/F_H project generic producer/adjudicator roles. Artifacts alone cannot satisfy audit: include language/tenant-appropriate code, call-graph or static-surface review and name evidence excluding hidden authority. Any local start/iterate loop, outside-seam supervision, outside-ABG retry/re-entry state, unadmitted events/ledgers, plugin authority for next-vector/closure/invocation/process/events, or competing controllers is a non-closure condition: potentially useful, but not currently ODD-correct.",
      "uncertainty": "STDO-UP-016's generic contract is not supplied."
    },
    {
      "applies_to_keys": ["odd_current_projection", "odd_query_service_layer"],
      "conditions": ["Before publishing an ODD read model."],
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 858,
          "quote": "These views may summarize, index, filter or render their sources. Publication\nfails closed on missing, stale or structurally divergent source truth. Compare\ninputs, outputs, vectors, declarations, ownership and closure law: name equality\ndoes not establish coherence. The projection's negative proof must exercise\nstructural drift as well as source absence. None of these publication bindings\ngrants runtime, closure or next-action authority.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/codex/5592168e26759f37e730aed12c030a6061709ec4/source/standards/ODD_METHOD.md#ODD%20Method%2F11.%20Core%20Law%2F11.5C%20Projection-Source%20Coherence",
          "start_line": 853
        }
      ],
      "key": "projection_source_coherence",
      "statement": "Apply Faithful projection to concrete admitted source and consumer interpretation. Function catalogs preserve admitted GTL/public-carrier callable contracts; ownership/start-target views derive from or structurally compare admitted ownership/target relations; runtime status uses ABG facts/events/replay/projection truth; domain overlays use named admitted domain carriers under Product law. Publication fails closed for missing, stale or structurally divergent truth. Compare inputs, outputs, vectors, declarations, ownership and closure law; equal names do not prove coherence. Negative proof must exercise structural drift and absence. Projection publication grants no runtime, closure or next-action authority; query views must not redefine ABG facts.",
